# Runtime output — regenerated by every scrape. Committing this shipped stale
# test data to fresh clones, which the server then served as if it were current.
data/current_listings.json

# Regenerable caches. Two are deliberately NOT here, for the same reason:
#  · data/geocode_cache.json — the 26 area coordinates never change, so having
#    them committed means a fresh clone (and the scheduled Actions run) skips
#    ~26 geocoding lookups entirely.
#  · data/grocery_cache.json — Overpass throttles shared cloud IPs, so the
#    Actions runner is the one machine that can't reliably fetch it. Committing
#    a list gathered from a normal connection is what lets the published site
#    have shop dots at all. It carries its own 30-day expiry, so a stale
#    committed copy still gets refreshed whenever a fetch does succeed.
data/bike_route_cache.json
data/address_cache.json

# Scrape diagnostics, written by --debug
debug_page.html

# Python / virtualenv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
.venv/

# Local working notes and editor state — not part of the project
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
